From 419c6991e21c60b0480cc77eef466715f29308ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 00:43:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11/24] Rewrite the TUI exit "Continue" suggestion to
 `hivemind`
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The opencode TUI prints a `Continue  opencode -s <session-id>` line on
exit. Under hivemind, the user-facing CLI is `hivemind`, not `opencode`,
so we rewrite the literal so the suggested command actually works.

The literal is hardcoded — there is no plugin slot, event, env var, or
config seam that lets a TUI plugin override the line (verified against
upstream source). This patch is the only path that currently works and
is the originating motivation for the bun-vendored build.

Rebrand the OPENCODE wordmark + TUI logo to HIVEMIND

Replaces the two ASCII-art glyph sources in the opencode source tree
that the user sees: the static `wordmark` array used by the exit screen
(`cli/ui.ts`), and the `logo.left`/`logo.right` paired arrays used by
the home-screen `<Logo />` component (`cli/logo.ts`).

Replaces the work of the deprecated `opencode/plugins/branding.js` TUI
plugin with a native source-level patch.

The HIVEMIND art is taken from the original branding plugin (5 slash-
art lines). The wordmark is trimmed to 4 lines to match the existing
exit-message template that references `logo[0]..logo[3]`. The TUI
`<Logo />` component iterates `logo.left` so we put the full 5-line art
on the left and emit empty padding strings on the right; the existing
shadow-marker rendering still works on the empty strings (no-op).
